Etsuko: Ahhh... that was a good one...
Etsuko[set_branch, stream2]: Look at how it bleeds... so beautiful...
///stream2
Etsuko[notif, $50, kuronekosan, what's your favorite videogame?]: Haaaaaaa... feels ecstatic cutting in front of so many people...
Etsuko: I've always liked videogames where the protag can die in several ways.
Etsuko: Whenever I'd get overwhelmed, I would play those games just to see the protag die over and over again.
Etsuko: Neck-breaking, blown-into-smithereens-ing, shot-in-the-heart-ing, and more.
Etsuko: I could do that too... Just end it all...
Etsuko: I live quite a few stories high... it'd all be so quick
Etsuko: But I've endured! And with the ecstasy of strangers' attention, I don't need to die anymore!
Etsuko: I really like games with sexy female protags too!
Etsuko: Not 'cause I'd self-insert myself into them, and imagine I'm a sexy girl too, but cause they'd die!
Etsuko: I can't get to be all athletic and hot like, lets say, Lara Croft, so in trade, she gets to die!
Etsuko: Again and again!!!
Etsuko: I'd make her drown on purpose.
Etsuko[notif, nakukoroni, $100,  cutcutcutcutcutcutcutcutcutcutcutcut]: Just to watch her gasp for air!
->Cut: set_branch, cut3
->Don't cut: set_branch, game_over
///cut3
Etsuko[set_branch, stream3|notif, inkcel01, $80, Are you single?]: Ahhhh....
///stream3
Etsuko: Yeah, I'm single!
Etsuko: Love's more than a drug to me, it's more like oxygen... I depend on it.
Etsuko: If there was liquid love, I'd inject so much of it into me.
Etsuko: I did have a boyfriend, once.
Etsuko: I thought he was such a nice guy at first.
Etsuko: I explained that I'm really mentally ill, and he stayed anyway.
Etsuko: That attention is more important than even eating to me, and I'd be annoyingly clingy.
Etsuko: It was all fine at the start, but...
Etsuko: As time went on, he'd respond less frequently, and give more dryer responses.
Etsuko: And I'd worry that I was an annoyance, a burden to him.
Etsuko: The thoughts of being hated by the person I loved so dearly got more and more intense, I was going insane.
Etsuko: I distracted myself from these thoughts by cutting myself all the time.
Etsuko: I wanted him to understand, to feel the pain I did, I even showed him my scars, how much I cut myself over him.
Etsuko: I showed how much I broke down over him, how much I loved him, how much I hated the thought of him hating me.
Etsuko: My life revolved around him, he was my everything!!!
Etsuko: But I guess I was just disposable to him...
Etsuko: Because he left me anyway. 
Etsuko: It's funny, he knew how I was like, 'cause I told him and stuff, and yet he left me and was, in the end, far from accomodating.
Etsuko: He said it was fine, but I guess not.
Etsuko: I wonder if he wanted me to suffer.
Etsuko: It took me so long to move on. And I felt like I deserved all the pain.
Etsuko: The question wasn't if I deserved it, but what I did to deserve it; what did I do that made everything go so downhill.
Etsuko[notif, madonanami, $1000, cut yourself 10 times ^o^]: I'm so surprised I didn't end up killing myself over him. I'm somehow still here after all that I went through.
